// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_instashield_frames.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: the insta-shield's S3K-derived animation gate — script_display_frames()
// in games/sonic4/player/player_instashield.emp, the fn both shipped ensures fold
// their scripts through.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "INSTASHIELD_POISON: a 3-frame script shows 3 display frames"
//
// The shipped guard compares OUR script's fold to the DONOR script's fold, so the
// only way it can be wrong is for the walker itself to be wrong — and there is one
// specific way it can be. S3K terminates with `$FD, 0`: a control code followed by an
// ARGUMENT byte that is itself a legal frame index. A walker that filters `byte <
// AF_SET_FIELD` instead of STOPPING at the first control byte counts that argument as
// an extra frame and reports 15 where the reference shows 14 — which is exactly the
// error this parcel made once, in the Python half, before it was caught.
//
// So this poison feeds a 3-frame script with S3K's two-byte terminator and demands a
// number the walker cannot produce. The fragment quotes the interpolated 3: a walker
// that counted the terminator's argument would print 4 and the case would NOT match,
// and one that returned a constant would print neither.
//
// AF_SET_FIELD is imported HERE as well as in player_instashield: a comptime helper's
// free names resolve at the CALL SITE (docs/EMP_PITFALLS.md §2), so the poison must
// carry the vocabulary the fn body spells.
//
// Zero bytes, ensures-only — unreachable from any real entry; evaluated only by
// tools/emp_expect_fail.py via `sigil build --extra-entry`.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_instashield_frames

use engine.constants.{AF_CHANGE, AF_SET_FIELD}
use games.sonic4.player_instashield.{script_display_frames}

// Three frames at S3K's hold of 0, then S3K's own `$FD, 0` terminator.
const POISON_SCRIPT: [u8; 6] = [0, 0, 1, 2, AF_CHANGE, 0]

// 14 is the reference's count; a 3-frame script cannot reach it.
const POISON_REFERENCE_FRAMES = 14

ensure(script_display_frames(POISON_SCRIPT, 6) == POISON_REFERENCE_FRAMES,
       "INSTASHIELD_POISON: a 3-frame script shows {script_display_frames(POISON_SCRIPT, 6)} display frames, not the reference {POISON_REFERENCE_FRAMES}")
